ase 1 trial. The company's partners and collaborators ApolloBio Corporation, AstraZeneca, Coherus Biosciences, Defense Advanced Research Projects Agency, HIV Vaccines Trial Network, Kaneka Eurogentec, National Institutes of Health, National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, Plumbline Life Sciences, Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Richter BioLogics, the University of Pennsylvania, and The Wistar Institute. The company was incorporated in 1983 and is headquartered in Plymouth Meeting, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Jacqueline E. Shea Ph.D. | CEO, President & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $889,099 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 112 people. Revenue per employee of $583 ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue falling 30%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $34K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1524\u00d7 revenue per employee (very high relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Inovio Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $330M market cap on $65,343 of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -81% over the past three years and -47% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -488% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $89M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 10.6% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 5748% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 0/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-33.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (22.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 132871% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 84/100): structural revenue/margin decline; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 124% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (20.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Inovio Pharmaceuticals (INO) Stock Gets Fair Value Boost After VOCERYQ Approval","